{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/994963-black-spiral-hive","id":994963,"title":"Black Spiral Hive","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-28T17:22:15-07:00","id":994963,"title":"Black Spiral Hive","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> I have a group of experienced players (we've been gaming on and off for about 20 years together) and one of them is playing a Shadow Lord. We are playing a game set in the 1870's in the Dakotas, for reference. The culmination of this next few months of gameplay will be the attack on a hive. While I've introduced BSD's in the past, I have not had an occasion where players actually ENTER a hive and if they decide to do so, I want to make it a horrific experience. The basic idea that I had was that the hive itself was a progressive descent into evil and the players would be walking the spiral (unless they were careful and aware) by progressing deeper and deeper. Some of the imagery I had that gave me this idea were the catacombs in the film As Above/So Below and I want to convey that same sense of weirdness in a place where they don't fully understand what's going on at first. Mostly, I want to move past the idea of legions of splatterfest minions to wade through and make this memorable. There is a theme so far in the story that follows the &quot;Road to hell is paved with good intentions&quot; saying, and it has led to some interesting moral dilemmas in the group. <br /> <br /> Can anyone help me out with some ideas that aren't my own? What things could be found in a hive? What else would make this better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12334-chemscout","name":"Chemscout","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T18:01:14-07:00","id":994985,"title":"","content":"Hives, like caerns, have an umbral aspect so feel free to come up with any weird things you'd like that may only work with &quot;dream logic&quot; or &quot;magical thinking&quot; as opposed to physical reality restrictions or logic.<br /> <br /> What kind of Hive is it? What is its Wyrm spirit purpose? That would help people think of appropriate weirdness for it.<br /> <br /> In my experience the keys to this kind of thing are:<ul><li>evocative description</li> <li>choices that matter (their decisions affect gameplay/outcome)</li> <li>interesting villains</li> </ul>A theme like &quot;the road to hell is paved with good intentions&quot; is either a) despite their good intentions, they engage in ethically wrong behavior, or b) despite their good intentions, their ignorance of what they are doing causes more problems than it solves. So which one best fits your game? Those are two different kinds of feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:07:00-07:00","id":995035,"title":"","content":"When I say &quot;the road to hell...&quot; I was referring to the idea that all of the characters (spiral or otherwise) think they are acting for reasons that are &quot;good&quot; (as they see it). So the Shadow Lord who has started leaning towards the wyrm has come down this path out of a desire to seek more power to prevent something worse from happening. <br /> <br /> As far as the hive spirits, that's a good idea. I'm not actually sure. I'll need to give it some thought. I've never had a Nexus Crawler in the game, and I thought to include one at some point. I do like the idea of &quot;dream logic&quot; though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12334-chemscout","name":"Chemscout","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T22:06:58-07:00","id":996452,"title":"","content":"I use BSD sparingly at best, but the current chronicle I'm writing will be featuring a BSD Hive.<br /> <br /> Stats of the Hive as of planning stage: Hive Level 2, The Hive of Burning Flesh. Type Stamina, Totem Green Dragon, Packs 4.<br /> Physical Description: A desolate area swept by periodic floods, the entrance to the forgotten Silver Mine lies behind a grove of sickly looking pine trees, the waste pile of the mine blocks off a series of ruined buildings that house a few kinfolk of the BSD and living quarters for the BSD packs. The buildings being used as living quarters are in far better shape than the outside looks.<br /> The mine houses the Caern the heart of which lies at the base of the shaft. Silver and iron pyrite veins still shine on the surface of the mine tunnels the tunnels lead downward. The central shaft must be reached by traveling through the winding upper level to the central shaft. The central shaft goes 1500 feet down no light is visible. In the Umbra toxic banes swarm the waste pile, the mine tunnels blaze with balefire torches and when opened the roars of Green Dragon can be heard echoing through the mine. The only way to access the Heart is to climb down the central shaft and is in a way a pilgramage, each level of the mine can only be accessed from a different side. Example: The second level is 25 feet down from the surface to reach the third level the Central Shaft must be reentered by circling through the tunnels and coming out the opposite side of the entrance. The only clue as to where the shaft can be entered is to follow the veins of silver when the vein vanishes the next tunnel leads to the proper entrance to the Central Shaft. The floor of the mine is laced with raw silver and burns all who walk upon it when the Heart of the Caern is opened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T01:32:32-07:00","id":996496,"title":"","content":"In my mind's eye, the &quot;Heart&quot; of a Black Spiral Dancer Hive bears a striking resemblance to the heart of the Atmosphere Processing Reactor of Hadley's Hope, designed by HR-Giger: A bio-mechanical nightmare of resin, slime, chitin and mucous wrought by a mad sculptor in the fashion of the bones and entrails of a giant, the walls themselves more flesh-than-stone, as if it is congealed corruption vomited forth from the ground itself by a dying God.<br /> <br /> Would that be an appropriate way to describe what a Black Spiral Dancer Hive's interior looks like to a First Time Werewolf Player? With James Horner's slow and eerily quiet-and-menacing musical score playing in the background meanwhile? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T13:35:01-07:00","id":998417,"title":"","content":"Those are actually really great ideas! I'm going to take a page from both of you, if you don't mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12334-chemscout","name":"Chemscout","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:43:15-07:00","id":998611,"title":"","content":"I have no problem with anyone using anything I post. The Mine I mentioned is an actual combination of the Pequea Silver Mine and the mine still open in Centraillia. The coal mines of Centraillia are the basis for Silent Hill. It is a depressing story, but an interesting place to visit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}